course: dictionary
lesson: 10210
title: Tiredness and your body
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tiredness is the feeling of needing rest or sleep. Your body tells you when it is running low on energy, and it is wise to listen. «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» Here tiredness is one sign that your body is fighting an illness.
explain: Tiredness often has causes you can change. Not enough sleep is the most common one. Children aged 9 to 10 need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep each night. Too much screen time before bed, illness and hard exercise can also leave you tired.
explain: Tiredness makes learning harder. When you are tired, it is hard to pay attention, to remember things and to keep calm. «Overcome by tiredness» means so tired that you cannot keep going. If you often feel this way, tell a grown-up.
explain: Tiredness can also make accidents more likely. A tired driver may not notice danger in time, which is why drivers need rest. A little tiredness for a day or two after a jab is normal, but tiredness that does not go away needs a grown-up's help.
fact: Tiredness means the feeling of needing rest or sleep.
fact: «Tiredness» is a noun with no plural, so you never write «tirednesses».
fact: Children aged 9 to 10 need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep each night.
fact: Causes of tiredness include not enough sleep, too much screen time before bed, illness and hard exercise.
fact: Dehydration, which means losing too much water and salts, can also cause tiredness.
exercise: Which of these is a common cause of tiredness? | Reading a book in the morning | *Not enough sleep | Eating a healthy lunch | Having a bath after school
exercise: What does tiredness mean? | Being hungry | A type of sleep | A feeling of being very happy | *The feeling of needing rest or sleep
exercise: Why is tiredness a danger for a driver? | *A tired driver may not notice danger in time | Tiredness makes the car lighter | Tiredness only affects people on bikes | A tired driver drives faster
test: «Dehydration means losing too much water and salts; signs are a dry mouth, dark or little wee, no tears, dizziness and tiredness.» Which is not a sign of dehydration? | Dry mouth | *Shiny, bright eyes | Dizziness | Dark or little wee
test: «Boredom is sometimes mixed with other feelings, like tiredness or loneliness.» What helps you deal with a mixed feeling? | *Naming the real feeling | Ignoring it until it goes away | Pretending it is not there | Shouting at someone
exam: Which sentence uses tiredness correctly? | *Tiredness made it hard for me to pay attention. | Tiredness are a feeling I like. | Tirednesses came in the bag. | I tiredness feel at school.
